+### "The app feels slow / I want to see how much memory it is using"
+
+**Settings → 📊 Memory** shows the live memory the running app is using and what is loaded right now — route waypoints and legs, notes, the flown track being recorded, and the navigation overlays (reporting points, airfields, VOR/DME stations, NOTAMs). It reads nothing saved and clears nothing; **Refresh** re-measures. The used-of-limit bar at the top is the browser’s JavaScript heap, which only Chrome and Android report — on iPhone and iPad the bar is replaced by a note that the figure is not available, and the counts below still work. This is the live counterpart to **💾 Storage**, which measures what is *saved* on the device.
+
 ## Reporting a bug
 
 1. Check the [open issues](https://github.com/msupino/NavigationApp/issues).
